\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces A fire crossing a ridge, from a 96.6\,GB simulation on a remote server, opened in ParaView. Outside the white box: Sieve{}'s overview, every timestep at every eighth grid point (47\,MB). Inside it: the time window and the region the scientist chose on that overview, fetched at full resolution (0.36\,GB) by the request shown (top right). Sieve{} explains each output in a provenance record (bottom right, excerpt). Both outputs carry the positions of their grid points, so ParaView places the detail inside the overview with no alignment step. \textbf  {[TODO: confirm the rendered timestep and the encodings: terrain colored by fuel left, the fire as a temperature surface, lines inside the box as streamlines of the full-resolution wind.]}}}{3}{figure.16}\protected@file@percent }
